# =============================================================================
# Store — UPDATE requests (VS Code REST Client) — PUT /api/v1/stores/{id} (ADMIN)
# =============================================================================
# Semantics: PARTIAL update — absent fields are LEFT UNCHANGED (nulls
# ignored). Present-but-empty strings are honored. When contact IS present
# it must be complete (replaced as a whole unit).
#
# Rules since ticket 0010:
#   - PUT on a CLOSED store → 404 (dead stores are immutable).
#   - PUT cannot set status to CLOSED → 400 (closing is DELETE's job; DELETE
#     owns the seat-release and the audit copy — one door to close).
#   - Other statuses via PUT stay legal (BLOCKED = temporarily not trading,
#     still visible and maintainable).
#
# How to run:
#   1. Start the backend: `docker compose up -d --build` — http://localhost:4000
#   2. Click the "Send Request" CodeLens above any request, IN ORDER, in one
#      sitting (captures are session-scoped).
#
# Prerequisites: the admin persona (see http/store/delete.http header for
# the SQL promotion one-liner).
#
# Notes:
#   - All data is FAKE (devtunde.com emails, Nigerian numbers).
#   - The automated suite for these endpoints: StoreApiTests (src/test/java).
#   - Re-runnable: manager personas, brands and contact emails are minted
#     fresh each run with {{$timestamp}} — no 409 collisions with prior runs.
#   - Access tokens expire after 15 MINUTES. If tokened requests suddenly 401,
#     re-send the SETUP requests from the top (they mint and re-capture).
#   - REST Client captures die on file/VS Code reopen. If you see raw {{...}}
#     template text being sent or sudden 500s, re-send the setup requests
#     from the top — never continue on a dead capture.
#   - Expected codes: 200 updated, 400 ghost admin/bad storeType/CLOSED via
#     PUT, 401 no/invalid token, 403 non-admin, 404 unknown or closed store,
#     204 close, 405 wrong method.
# =============================================================================

@storeUrl = http://localhost:4000/api/v1/stores
@authUrl = http://localhost:4000/api/v1/auth

### 1 — Setup: login the admin persona
# Expected: 200
# @name adminLogin
POST {{authUrl}}/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "admin@devtunde.com",
  "password": "Password123!"
}

### 2 — Setup: signup the store manager (minted fresh each run)
# Expected: 201
# @name sellerSignup
POST {{authUrl}}/signup
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "Updatable Manager",
  "email": "probe-update-mgr-{{$timestamp}}@devtunde.com",
  "password": "Password123!",
  "phone": "+2348031234582"
}

### 3 — Setup: login the manager
# Expected: 200
# @name sellerLogin
POST {{authUrl}}/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{sellerSignup.response.body.user.email}}",
  "password": "Password123!"
}

### 4 — Setup: create a store to update (minted brand)
# Expected: 201
# @name createStore
POST {{storeUrl}}
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{adminLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

{
  "brand": "Updatable Store {{$timestamp}}",
  "description": "Before the update",
  "storeType": "BRANCH",
  "storeAdminPublicId": "{{sellerLogin.response.body.user.publicId}}",
  "contact": {
    "address": "12 Market Road, Lagos",
    "phone": "08012345678",
    "email": "updatable-{{$timestamp}}@devtunde.com"
  }
}

### 5 — Update the brand ONLY
# Expected: 200 — brand changed; description/storeType/status/contact untouched
PUT {{storeUrl}}/{{createStore.response.body.publicId}}
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{adminLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

{
  "brand": "Rebranded Store {{$timestamp}}"
}

### 6 — Update the description only
# Expected: 200
PUT {{storeUrl}}/{{createStore.response.body.publicId}}
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{adminLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

{
  "description": "After the update"
}

### 7 — Block the store via status
# Expected: 200 — status BLOCKED (alive-but-not-trading: still visible and
# still maintainable; the catalog's trading gate is a separate rule)
PUT {{storeUrl}}/{{createStore.response.body.publicId}}
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{adminLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

{
  "status": "BLOCKED"
}

### 8 — Try to CLOSE the store via PUT
# Expected: 400 — "Store closure not permitted". Closing has exactly one
# door: DELETE /api/v1/stores/{id} (it releases the admin's seat and fills
# the audit column — PUT would silently skip both)
PUT {{storeUrl}}/{{createStore.response.body.publicId}}
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{adminLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

{
  "status": "CLOSED"
}

### 9 — Setup: signup a reassign target (minted fresh each run)
# Expected: 201
# @name secondSignup
POST {{authUrl}}/signup
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "Reassign Target",
  "email": "probe-reassign-{{$timestamp}}@devtunde.com",
  "password": "Password123!",
  "phone": "+2348031234583"
}

### 10 — Setup: login the reassign target
# Expected: 200
# @name secondLogin
POST {{authUrl}}/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{secondSignup.response.body.user.email}}",
  "password": "Password123!"
}

### 11 — Reassign the store admin
# Expected: 200 — storeAdminPublicId is now the target's
PUT {{storeUrl}}/{{createStore.response.body.publicId}}
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{adminLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

{
  "storeAdminPublicId": "{{secondLogin.response.body.user.publicId}}"
}

### 12 — Reassign to a ghost admin
# Expected: 400 — "Store admin not found" (payload problem, NOT a 404)
PUT {{storeUrl}}/{{createStore.response.body.publicId}}
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{adminLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

{
  "storeAdminPublicId": "11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111"
}

### 13 — Unknown store id
# Expected: 404 — "Store not found"
PUT {{storeUrl}}/99999999-9999-9999-9999-999999999999
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{adminLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

{
  "brand": "No Such Store"
}

### 14 — No Authorization header
# Expected: 401
PUT {{storeUrl}}/{{createStore.response.body.publicId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "brand": "Tokenless Update"
}

### 15 — Setup: signup the regular persona (fixed — she never holds a seat)
# Expected: 201 (409 if she already exists — either way the account exists)
# @name regularSignup
POST {{authUrl}}/signup
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "Bola Storeless",
  "email": "bola.storeless@devtunde.com",
  "password": "Password123!",
  "phone": "+2348031234571"
}

### 16 — Setup: login the regular persona
# Expected: 200
# @name regularLogin
POST {{authUrl}}/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "bola.storeless@devtunde.com",
  "password": "Password123!"
}

### 17 — Update as a regular user
# Expected: 403 — updates are admin-only
PUT {{storeUrl}}/{{createStore.response.body.publicId}}
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{regularLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

{
  "brand": "Regular User Update"
}

### 18 — Unknown storeType in the body
# Expected: 400, never 500 — the enum rejects it at deserialization
PUT {{storeUrl}}/{{createStore.response.body.publicId}}
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{adminLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

{
  "storeType": "MALL"
}

### 19 — Empty body is a legal no-op
# Expected: 200 — store returned unchanged (all-null update, nulls ignored)
PUT {{storeUrl}}/{{createStore.response.body.publicId}}
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{adminLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

{}

### 20 — Close the store (the ONE legal closing door)
# Expected: 204 — status → CLOSED; the admin's seat is released
DELETE {{storeUrl}}/{{createStore.response.body.publicId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

### 21 — Update the CLOSED store
# Expected: 404 — dead stores are immutable; even the admin gets honest-404
PUT {{storeUrl}}/{{createStore.response.body.publicId}}
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{adminLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

{
  "description": "Necromancy attempt"
}
